{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781398582,"nonce":"Qzp/rmLEAp1SimKe7RWDMAN7lX4=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABFZtbJQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/266","origin":"github"},"title":"Activate reflex confidence floor on BizzyBoat (obstacle_prob_min: 0.60)","message":"## Summary\n\nActivate the reflex confidence floor on BizzyBoat by passing **`obstacle_prob_min: 0.60`** to the\n`segments_to_pointcloud_reflex` include in `bizzyboat_project11/launch/perception_launch.py`.\n\nThe capability (rolker/unh_marine_perception#35) and the launch argument\n(rolker/unh_marine_perception#37) are merged; this sets the validated BizzyBoat value so the\nreflex e-stop stops reacting to low-confidence calm-water reflections.\n\n## Why 0.60 (\"Balanced\")\n\nFrom the 2026-06-12 analysis: cloud reflections read ~0.55 confidence vs real buoys/pots\n0.85–0.98. The offline regression harness showed a 0.60 floor roughly halves reflex false stops\nwhile keeping buoys, pot floats, and most debris (the debris-preserving default Roland chose). The\noperator can raise to ~0.75 (\"Suppress-reflection\") on glassy water via `ros2 param set`. The\neWaSR retrain (rolker/unh_marine_perception#34) remains the durable fix for high-confidence bright\nreflections.\n\n## Change\n- `bizzyboat_project11/launch/perception_launch.py`: add `'obstacle_prob_min': '0.60'` to the\n  reflex include's `launch_arguments`.\n\n## After merge\nBoat needs `git pull` + relaunch (no rebuild — launch-only change) to pick it up. Verify:\n`ros2 param get /bizzy/oak_forward/segments_to_pointcloud_reflex obstacle_prob_min` -\u003e 0.60.\n\n## Related\n- rolker/unh_marine_perception#35 (capability), #37 (launch arg), #34 (retrain), #30 (radar UI)\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Fable 5`","files":null}]}